Hold back enet_peer_disconnect_now() like GFE's reliable disconnect so a queued termination
message is still delivered. Sunshine forks send their end message and disconnect at once.
Only a disconnect that passes ENet's own peer ID, peer state and session ID checks is held
back, so a stale or stray disconnect datagram that ENet would drop cannot end the stream.
On stop, a host whose disconnect was held back is released at once instead of lingering for
an acknowledgement it never sends, and the intercept is removed before a graceful linger so
a host disconnect that arrives during it ends the linger.
Applies after host-termination.patch.

